 "text": "Same thousand dollars, same S&P 500. One friend ends with ten times as much. Guess what the other two did? They buy in at the start of two thousand and six. The two thousand and eight crash shrinks each one to seven hundred and seventy. One new phone. Jay panics, sells, and hides the cash in a shoebox. Maya sells too, then buys back a year later. Sam holds and lets his dividends reinvest. By twenty thirteen, Sam's money is worth over two phones. Jay's shoebox? Still one. By twenty nineteen, over four phones. Jay? Still one. End of twenty twenty-five, Sam's at over ten phones, about eight thousand dollars. Jay? Still one. And Maya? Same as Sam, except one year. About eight phones. That one missed year cost her two. So if your money crashed tomorrow, would you sell, wait, or hold?",
